11
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
The Untouchables is a 1987 American crime film directed by Brian De
Palma, produced by Art Linson and written by David Mamet.

12
01:04:54,545 --> 01:05:00,545
It stars Kevin Costner, Charles Martin Smith, Andy
García, Robert De Niro and Sean Connery.

13
01:10:19,090 --> 01:10:25,090
Set in 1930 Chicago, the film follows Eliot Ness (Costner) as he forms the
Untouchables team to bring Al Capone (De Niro) to justice during Prohibition.

14
01:15:43,636 --> 01:15:49,636
It is the third film on which De Niro and De Palma collaborated, after
Greetings (De Niro's first lead in a feature role) and Hi, Mom!.

15
01:21:08,181 --> 01:21:14,181
The screenplay is loosely based on Ness's and Oscar Fraley's 1957 book The Untouchables and the
real-life events on which it is based, although most of its plot is fictionalized.

16
01:26:32,727 --> 01:26:38,727
The Grammy Award-winning score is composed by Ennio Morricone
and features period music by Duke Ellington.

17
01:31:57,272 --> 01:32:03,272
The Untouchables premiered on June 2, 1987, in New York City, and went
into general release on June 3, 1987, in the United States.

18
01:37:21,818 --> 01:37:27,818
The film grossed $106.2 million worldwide and received
generally positive reviews from critics.

19
01:42:46,363 --> 01:42:52,363
It was nominated for four Academy Awards; Connery won the Academy Award for Best Supporting
Actor, as well as the Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor – Motion Picture.

20
01:48:10,909 --> 01:48:16,909
The film explores themes of chicago, illinois, prohibition
era, gangster, baseball bat, white suit.

21
01:53:35,454 --> 01:53:41,454
The tone is intense.
